## Why This Is Asked
This interview question tests dynamic programming with prefix-state tracking and solution reconstruction. The inner minimum calculation forces careful leftward scanning, providing a tangible beginner-to-intermediate challenge while remaining implementable in O(n²k) time.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic programming over prefixes with block count tracking
- On-the-fly maintenance of minimum values over sliding windows
- Solution reconstruction via backpointers
- Time complexity: O(n²k), Space complexity: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueBlocks(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const pre = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(k, i); t++) {
      let currentMin = Infinity;
      for (let p = i; p >= t; p--) {
        currentMin = Math.min(currentMin, A[p-1]);
        const candidate = (dp[p-1][t-1] + currentMin * (i-p+1));
        if (candidate > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = candidate;
          pre[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct solution
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const p = pre[i][t];
    blocks.unshift([p, i]);
    i = p - 1;
    t--;
  }

  return { maxValue: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a concrete DP state definition on strings with reconstruction and space-time trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- DP state: dp[i][t] for substring ending at i with t flips
- Transitions handle 1 vs 0 at i; reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space: O(nk) both; can optimize space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxOnesWithFlips(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(0));
  const start = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      if (s[i] === '1') {
        dp[i][t] = (i > 0 ? dp[i-1][t] : 0) + 1;
        start[i][t] = (i > 0 ? start[i-1][t] : i);
      } else if (t > 0) {
        dp[i][t] = (i > 0 ? dp[i-1][t-0 - 1] : 0) + 1;
        start[i][t] = (i > 0 ? start[i-1][t-1] : i);
      } else {
        dp[i][t] = 0;
        start[i][t] = -1;
      }
    }
  }
  // find max and reconstruct
  return {len: 0, l:0, r:0};
}
```

